    "body": "Parent: #122\nSource: PDF §§14-17.\n\nConsolidate the formal analysis into a versioned monograph/design document that can serve as the long-lived research and engineering reference.\n\n## Proposed structure\n\n1. Problem statement and non-goals.\n2. Semantic state spaces and holographic projections.\n3. Graph induction from teacher behavior.\n4. Predictive entropy, semantic compression, and information bottleneck.\n5. Semantic operating system architecture.\n6. Future-state optimization and bounded planning.\n7. Compiler stages and reference intermediate representation.\n8. Boolean/integer lowering and R4G1 artifact format.\n9. Runtime execution model and resource contract.\n10. Structural proofs and proof-status matrix.\n11. Empirical certification, statistical protocol, and negative results.\n12. Rust module map, migration plan, and open research questions.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The document links every normative definition to its implementation issue/module and every guarantee to its evidence artifact.\n- Structural guarantees, empirical measurements, and research hypotheses are visually and terminologically distinct.\n- It records known negative results and non-goals, including no exact-equivalence or human-level reasoning claim.\n- It includes a dependency graph for the implementation issues and a migration path that preserves the legacy transformerless artifacts.\n- A review checklist verifies consistency with the PDF, implementation plan, R4G1 RFC, threat model, and proof-status matrix.",
